  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the API**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the API design for using the \'gemini-3.7-flash\' model. I\'ll instantiate the GoogleGenAI client with the `new GoogleGenAI({})` constructor, and I\'m developing the logic for graceful fallback if the API key is missing or there\'s an API error. I\'ll need to define the structure of requests and responses for optimal integration.\n\n\n**Integrating Vite and Express**\n\nI\'m now diving into integrating Vite and Express. I\'m considering using Vite\'s dev server with a custom plugin or proxy for the Express backend on port 3001, OR an Express app integrating Vite middleware. I\'m leaning toward the `server.ts` approach using Express + Vite middleware, potentially running on port 3000. It seems the ideal setup for full-stack Node/Express + React apps. I\'m focusing on how `package.json` configurations manage the port startup and building this in the production environment. This should provide a single process with one command for the development experience and build process.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mangrove Zones**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing specific mangrove zones for assessment. I have data for several areas, including the Odisha delta at 2,450 ha, Andhra Pradesh\'s Coringa Wildlife Sanctuary at 1,800 ha, the Andaman Islands\' Baratang & Havelock at 1,650 ha, and Gujarat\'s Gulf of Kutch at 3,100 ha. This initial step is key to forming a structured approach.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Constructing the MRV Pipeline**\n\nNow I\'m building the Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) pipeline with a multi-source approach. I\'m leveraging Sentinel-2 & Landsat-9 imagery, plus drone telemetry, and in-situ IoT ground stations. The imagery will offer NDVI, EVI, and SAR backscatter data, and the drones provide canopy models and stand density. Ground stations will deliver crucial soil data. It feels like a robust plan.\n\n\n**Validating the Data**\n\nI\'m now verifying data with a multi-tiered Byzantine fault tolerance check. I\'m focusing on comparing above-ground and below-ground carbon estimates from satellites, drones, and ground stations. I\'m establishing variance thresholds to identify discrepancies and performing sensor sanity checks. I can confirm a consensus with a high confidence score if validated. Conversely, it alerts for anomalies and ensures no credits are minted if there\'s a problem.\n\n\n\n**Calculating Carbon Metrics**\n\nI\'m presently working out the carbon metrics. I\'m calculating total carbon, factoring in above-ground biomass, below-ground biomass, and soil organic carbon. Then, I\'ll determine the CO2 equivalent, considering area and sequestration period, and finally, deduct uncertainty and baseline risk. I need to make sure the math is sound.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 698364510
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
