  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial architecture. I\'ve started outlining the backend, specifically `server.ts`, which will use Express and run on port 3000.  The plan is to have `/api/*` endpoints. Right now, I\'m thinking of `/api/sites` to retrieve mangrove site data, including sensor readings, drone imagery, and satellite data, along with geo-coordinates and species mix. I\'ll also need a `/api/sites/:id` endpoint for individual sites.\n\n\n**Expanding API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out specific API endpoints. I\'ve added `/api/mrv/verify` for consensus calculations and ledger interactions, plus endpoints for simulating degradation and managing credits. I\'m also including detailed ledger management APIs: verification, tamper simulation, repair, and credit-specific actions. Further, I\'m considering endpoints for AI analysis and a reset function. The Express framework remains central.\n\n\n**Integrating Vite Development**\n\nNow I\'m integrating Vite with `server.ts` for a unified development environment. Running `npm run dev` or `npm start` will execute `tsx server.ts` and serve both the API and the React SPA. In production, it\'ll serve static assets from the `dist` folder. I\'ve updated the `package.json` scripts to reflect this change. I\'m also ensuring the necessary dependencies for the front-end are installed. My next step will be designing the domain models.\n\n\n**Establishing Domain Types**\n\nI\'m now focusing on establishing the core domain types, which I\'ll put in `shared/types.ts` or `src/types/index.ts`. I\'m starting with a comprehensive `MangroveSite` type. It will include fields for IDs, names, coordinates, and various mangrove-specific attributes such as dominant species, ecosystem type, and health metrics. I\'m also adding fields for biomass, verification status, telemetry data from satellites, and credit-related values.\n\n\n**Defining Sensor Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing the structure for handling various sensor data. I\'ve created types to represent data from satellites, drones, and ground sensors. This includes specific measurements like canopy height, soil carbon, and salinity. These types will ensure the API can properly handle the diverse information gathered from the field.\n\n\n**Structuring Data Types**\n\nI\'m now focusing on detailing the data structures for key concepts. I\'ve defined `ConsensusResult` with fields like confidence scores and source agreement. Also added the `CarbonCredit` type, which includes status and vintage information. I\'ve included the logic needed to capture data for transactions, site details and verification. I\'ve also thought about how all of the data may be summarized.\n\n\n\n**Defining Ledger Block Data**\n\nI\'m now detailing the ledger data structures, specifically `LedgerBlock`, `LedgerVerificationResult`, and `BufferReserveSummary`. I\'m focusing on defining the properties for each, including block types, timestamps, and various data fields to capture information from credit minting to buffer reversals. Additionally, I\'m documenting the verification details with properties like `isValid` and `chainAudit`. Also, I\'m including `BufferReserveSummary` fields like `bufferRatioPct` and `solvencyRatioPct`. My current goal is to define how these data structures support the integrity of the ledger.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 294457826
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
