        lines {
          text: "          Traditional carbon markets collapsed in 2021-22 when tokenized credits (e.g. Toucan Protocol) backed degraded or burned forests without any physical reserves. The <strong>Blue Carbon Registry</strong> solves this by ring-fencing <strong>20% of all minted credits into a non-tradeable buffer pool</strong>. When natural disasters (cyclones, tidal surges, or dieback) degrade a mangrove zone, the system automatically burns buffer credits on-chain to cover the exact carbon delta \342\200\224 <strong>keeping tradeable market credits 100% solvent.</strong>"
