        }
        lines {
          text: "              \"Judges, in 2021-22, Web3 carbon tokenization platforms tokenized over 20 million carbon credits. But investigations found that <strong>over 28% were \'zombie credits\'</strong> \342\200\224 issued for forests that had already been clear-cut or double-counted years prior. Tokenizing bad data just makes carbon fraud faster. We solved the root cause: <strong>Real-time physical MRV consensus before minting, plus an automated Buffer Reserve pool</strong>.\""
